k\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T18:31:13-07:00","id":899627,"title":"","content":"I guess now Dog as I have 6 that I rescued around the streets of San Antonio. But I like Cats too, can I say I like animals as I really don't like to see any suffer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11846-atomichammer","name":"AtomicHammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T04:35:51-07:00","id":904085,"title":"","content":"Was a dog person, then got a cat. I love cats but I love dogs too. I suppose I'm both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T20:59:03-07:00","id":908091,"title":"","content":"I'm a cat person. Growing up . . . I didn't have the best experiences with dogs, so I have a hard time relaxing around them. But I love cats. I have two of my own, and I feed the several stray/feral ones in the area. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/892653-pet-lovers-which-are-you?p=893634#post893634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love cats, dislike dogs, though I've heard Shiba Inus are basically the exact kind of dog I'd want. They're basically a fluffy some-what fox looking cat. I have known multiple people with one and they say they act just like a cat. Very big on looking elegant/important. Somewhat aloof, especially to new people. Talkative in a way. Bit bitey if they feel you're not treating them respectfully. Very big on staying clean. Fluffy dogs are more ok with me. But fluffy cat hiding in a dog body? Win.</div> </div> </div> </div>My sister's Shih-Tzu is also a wannabe cat. He even likes playing with cat toys. Its interesting, though - he won't bat at them like a cat does. He just tries to bite them. Doesn't even occur to him to use his paws.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T13:44:05-07:00","id":911857,"title":"","content":"I'm going to take the third route and say I'm a rabbit person. But I love dogs too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],